WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.552
Standardization changes the numerical representation used by software.

00:00:04.552 --> 00:00:07.657
It does not change the conceptual measurement scale.

00:00:07.657 --> 00:00:10.107
Temperature remains an interval measurement.

00:00:10.107 --> 00:00:12.592
Emergency visits remains a count.

00:00:12.592 --> 00:00:19.577
In a real predictive workflow, fit the scaler on training data only and then apply the fitted scaler to

00:00:19.577 --> 00:00:24.632
validation and test data. That preserves the train-test boundary and avoids leakage.

00:00:24.632 --> 00:00:29.707
Preprocessing is not neutral: it tells software how to interpret the variable.

00:00:29.707 --> 00:00:35.877
One-hot encoding avoids inventing rank for nominal categories; ordinal coding preserves a known order;

00:00:35.877 --> 00:00:40.402
scaling changes numerical representation but not conceptual meaning.

00:00:40.402 --> 00:00:47.120
In predictive work, learned preprocessing should be fitted only on training data so evaluation remains honest.
